	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/markdown" rect="(80.0, 680.0, 760.0, 110.0)" font-family="Sans Serif" font-size="16">*Chapter 10. 10A: each tagger takes a few seconds, Stanza about a minute the first time. 10B: the Python Script keeps sentences whose root verb has a subject and an object; change the framework in the POS Tagger and compare. 10C: in Preprocess Text use the Regexp tokenizer (pattern [\w’]+, no Lowercase), then the POS Tagger stage (Averaged Perceptron), then the filter Filter by POS tags, and type the tags to keep (NN,NNS,NNP,NNPS).*</text>
	</annotations>
